invariant: INV-41
file: src/rsa_mont64.c
catches: rsa_equiv_test
reason: rsa_mont64_to_bytes writes the len % 8 bytes at the front of a
  number in the order of their weights, the lowest first, where the
  number is big-endian. A length that is a multiple of 8 has no such
  bytes, so every verification passes. bin/rsa_equiv_test holds the byte
  moves to the bytes that went in at every length.

--- old
        bytes[(len & 7) - 1 - i] = (uint8_t)(words[whole] >> (8 * i));
--- new
        bytes[i] = (uint8_t)(words[whole] >> (8 * i));
